围绕 sigaltstack 中 SS_AUTODISARM/SS_ONSTACK 的写法，Michael Kerrisk（man-pages）在正文中列出多条实践论据，其中第 4 条称 "Some implementations (including all the ones that I looked at the source code for, that is Illumos, FreeBSD, OpenBSD) explicitly error if ss.ss_flags has bits other than SS_DISABLE set"。本封 FROM Stas Sergeev 回应该条称 "Well, yes, those are the practical arguments that can't be ignored"，同时坚持 Linux 内核的这一实现并非出于误解，而是依 POSIX 文本最直白的读法作出，且仍接受 0，故不致单独造成兼容性问题。

