Kyle McMartin 在 flock/FAGAIN/FWOULDBLOCK 讨论中点明："flock is not POSIX, it's an interface invented by 4.2BSD, and was previously emulated by glibc. The glibc wrapper implemented flock with fcntl and made sure to return EWOULDBLOCK."——BSD 4.2 才是 flock 的接口源头。Matthew Wilcox 回复："glibc's emulation of flock() using fcntl() really belongs to the Dark Ages of Linux. According to the comments in the kernel, flock(2) was added in June 1995. That's four years before parisc-linux really got going. The semantics of flock-locks and fcntl-locks are really, really different. Emulating one with the other was a really bad idea."——将 glibc 模拟方式定性为 Linux 黑暗时代的遗留。此外 Matthew 建议以"#define EWOULDBLOCK EAGAIN"在 __KERNEL__ 中强制 EAGAIN，用 EAGAIN/EWOULDBLOCK 的历史包袱解释内核为何长期两码混用。

以上为邮件列表当事人一手自述/主张，属过程性证据，具体技术结论仍须以源码与提交记录复核为准，不得单独引为定论。【linux邮件提取】

