Theodore Ts'o（本封 FROM，署名「- Ted」）在 Linux-next 接口稳定性讨论中回应 Greg Kroah-Hartman——后者援引 Linus 的「Linux is evolution, not intelligent design」为其 flag-day 改造辩护，并自陈 kobject 迁移是其成功先例。Ts'o 指出该语录常被当作铁律推向极端（「no interface without an in-tree user」被用来约束函数参数、并被用来排斥任何前瞻性接口设计），随后在 L36-41 写明双向反对立场：「Clearly, we are right to mock Solaris for making claims that they will never, ever, *ever* change an interface, not even one that goes back sixteen years to Solaris 2.3. But it doesn't follow the opposite point of view, that constant mutability of kernel interfaces to make sure that things are always perfect and pure and clean is the right one either.」即嘲笑 Solaris 式绝对不变是对的，但由此反向推出接口必须持续翻烧饼同样不成立。他主张把旋钮「turn the knob back a quarter turn towards tolerating __deprecated old interfaces a little bit more」，让接口稳定度稍稍提高，并提议写一篇与 stable_api_nonsense.txt 相对的 unstable_api_nonsense.txt。

以上为邮件列表当事人一手自述/主张，属过程性证据，具体技术结论仍须以源码与提交记录复核为准，不得单独引为定论。【linux邮件提取】

