针对 close-on-fork 的 RFC——Nate Karstens 称已获 Austin Common Standards Revision Group 批准纳入下一版 POSIX——Al Viro 反对：该改动惩罚系统内每次 fork() 并增加内存占用与 API 复杂度。他说「the only authority it has ever had derives from consensus between existing Unices」，故「Solaris does it, Linux and *BSD do not」意味着「Austin Group is welcome to take a hike」；另指出 *BSD 无一实现该行为，并以 NAKed-by: Al Viro <viro@zeniv.linux.org.uk> 收尾。

